01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Dragonfly is a 2002 supernatural drama thriller film directed by Tom Shadyac from a screenplay by
Brandon Camp, Mike Thompson, and David Seltzer based on a story by Camp and Thompson.

11
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
The film was produced by Gary Barber, Roger Birnbaum, Mark Johnson, and Shadyac.

12
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
It stars Kevin Costner as a grieving doctor being contacted by his
dead wife through his patients' near-death experiences.

13
01:24:30,000 --> 01:24:36,000
Upon release, Dragonfly was a critical and commercial failure, with the film only grossing $52.3 million against its $60 million production
budget and was universally panned by critics, who described it as "sappy, dull and muddled" and "too melancholic and cliched".

